-- title:
--   Rational scalars that are products of Γ-conjugates lie in Γ
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_1,b_1$, a nonzero squarefree natural number $N$ and primes $q,q'$ with $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$, $q'\neq q$ and $q,q'\geq 5$. Assume `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a₁ b₁ q'`, that is $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1,R_1$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order (an order, i.e. containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, of full $\mathbb Q$-span and finitely generated, maximal among such) and $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection $\Lambda'\cap\Lambda''$ of two maximal orders with relative index $N$ in $\Lambda'$, and $R_1\leq\Lambda_1$. Let $v_2$ be a height-one prime containing $q$, and let $\Gamma\leq\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ be a subgroup whose members are exactly those $x$ lying in `awayUnits R₁ v₂` — for every height-one prime $w\neq v_2$ the image of $x$ in $(\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w)^\times$ lies in the subgroup generated by those units having both themselves and their inverse in [`Submodule.localBox R₁ w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) — and such that $\mathrm{padicValRat}\,q(\mathrm{nrd}\,x)$ is even, where $\mathrm{nrd}\,x=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a_1x_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-b_1x_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+a_1b_1x_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$. Then any unit $z$ which is the image of a nonzero rational scalar and which can be written $z=\delta\,(t^{-1}\gamma t)$ with $\delta,\gamma\in\Gamma$ and $t\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ arbitrary, itself lies in $\Gamma$.
--
--   This is the closure property of the group of $q$-units of even reduced-norm valuation in a definite quaternion algebra with Eichler order of squarefree level, used to control the scalars occurring in the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the relevant quotient. It is invoked in the faithfulness step [`CerednikDrinfeld.descentIntertwining_of_base_zero_one`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.descentIntertwining_of_base_zero_one), where an element acting trivially is exhibited as a rational scalar multiple of a conjugate of an element of $\Gamma$.
